 "script": {
  "hook": "A user taps ten times on a flight. Analytics must not lose a single tap.",
  "question": "Design an offline event queue.",
  "trap": "The trap: keep events in memory. A crash or a kill loses them all.",
  "steps": [
   "Persist first. Write every event to a local database with a sequence number.",
   "Drain in order. When the network returns, send the oldest events first, and stop at the first failure.",
   "Bound the queue. Cap its size and age. When full, drop the least important events first.",
   "Replay safely. Give each event an id and its original timestamp. The server drops duplicates and corrects clock skew."
  ],
  "takeaway": "Persist first, drain in order, cap it, replay idempotently.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: session and identity stitching.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
